<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 216 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mani was a Persian prophet of the third century CE and founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manichaeism">Manichaeism</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a>'s profile, he described Aksum as one of the four great powers of the world, alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. His statement is often cited as evidence of Aksum's international standing.</p></div>
